## Your work

Use the \`qa\` skill.

## Why this attempt

A previous session of this attempt ended without reporting (\`qa.died\`: launch_unknown). This is a fresh session: nothing it did counts as reported. Look at \`git status\`, \`git log\` and the handoff for partial work, then finish the step.

qa#1 reported \`fail\` on older code. Since then: implement.done → test.pass → review.approve. Do this step again in full on the current HEAD: what earlier attempts found or observed is history, not a result for this one.

## Finish with exactly one of

- \`norn done pass --criteria <file> --handoff "…"\` — every criterion verified with evidence
- \`norn done fail --criteria <file> --handoff "…"\` — a criterion fails; repro in the receipt
- \`norn done partial --criteria <file> --handoff "…"\` — criteria only a person can check are listed with prepared evidence
- \`norn ask "<question>"\` — you need a person's answer to continue; the step parks until answered
- \`norn stuck "<reason>"\` — you cannot continue; a person unblocks the step

\`--criteria <file>\`: a JSON array with one verdict per acceptance criterion — \`pass\` (with \`evidence\`), \`fail\` (with \`repro\`), \`person\` (with \`how\`), \`unverified\` (with \`reason\` and \`how\`). Worst verdict: fail > unverified > person > pass. Write the file outside the repository, next to your evidence (e.g. \`$TMPDIR/criteria.json\`); never under \`runs/\`.

One entry for each of these criteria, and no other id:

- \`AC1\` (verifier: agent)
- \`AC2\` (verifier: agent)

